T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare and contrast Verilog \(IEEE 1364\) versus SystemVerilog \(IEEE 1800\), explaining why modern semiconductor verification transitioned to SystemVerilog object-oriented programming \(OOP\), constrained randomization, and assertions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Limitations of Traditional Verilog-2001 in Verification:) Tj
T*
(   - IEEE 1364 Verilog was originally designed primarily as a hardware modeling and simulation) Tj
T*
(   language. It relies on static structural modules, wire/reg data types, and procedural blocks) Tj
T*
(   \(always, initial\).) Tj
T*
(   - As microchips expanded to billions of transistors, testbenches authored in Verilog suffered) Tj
T*
(   from severe structural limitations: testbench components were statically instantiated, could) Tj
T*
(   not be dynamically created or garbage collected, and lacked Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\)) Tj
T*
(   abstractions. Stimulus was overwhelmingly directed, meaning engineers manually authored) Tj
T*
(   specific test sequences that only verified anticipated bugs, leaving unexpected corner cases) Tj
T*
(   undiscovered.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. SystemVerilog \(IEEE 1800\) Architectural Paradigm Shift:) Tj
T*
(   - Unified Design and Verification: SystemVerilog integrates hardware design constructs \(logic) Tj
T*
(   data type, always_comb, always_ff, interfaces\) with advanced software verification) Tj
T*
(   capabilities.) Tj
T*
(   - Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\): Introduces dynamic classes, inheritance, polymorphism, and) Tj
T*
(   encapsulation. Testbench components \(drivers, monitors, scoreboards\) are modeled as reusable,) Tj
T*
(   modular objects instantiated dynamically during simulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Constrained-Random Stimulus \(CRV\): Verification engineers declare randomized transaction) Tj
T*
(   variables \(rand bit [31:0] addr, data\) paired with complex algebraic constraint blocks \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   constraint c_range { addr inside {[32'h1000:32'h2000]}; addr % 4 == 0; }\). Solvers) Tj
T*
(   automatically generate millions of unique, valid stimulus vectors.) Tj
T*
(   - Functional Coverage Closure: Integrates native covergroups, coverpoints, and cross-coverage) Tj
T*
(   to mathematically track whether all operational states, buffer boundaries, and protocol states) Tj
T*
(   have been thoroughly validated.) Tj
T*
(   - SystemVerilog Assertions \(SVA\): Temporal property specifications that continuously monitor) Tj
T*
(   internal protocol rules cycle-by-cycle \(e.g. assert property \(@\(posedge clk\) req |=> ##[1:3]) Tj
T*
(   grant\)\), catching bugs at their source rather than waiting for corrupted data to emerge) Tj
T*
(   hundreds of cycles later.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
