(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the architectural features, internal memory blocks, and development toolchain of AMD Xilinx FPGAs \(Artix-7 and Zynq-7000 SoC\), explaining LUTs, Flip-Flops, BRAMs, and DSP48 slices.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Reconfigurable Architecture of Xilinx 7-Series FPGAs:) Tj
T*
(   - Configurable Logic Blocks \(CLBs\): The primary logic resource in Xilinx FPGAs. Each 7-series) Tj
T*
(   CLB contains two slices \(SliceL - Logic or SliceM - Memory\).) Tj
T*
(   - 6-Input Look-Up Tables \(LUTs\): Each slice contains four 6-input LUTs. A 6-LUT can implement) Tj
T*
(   any arbitrary 6-input combinational boolean function or be split into two independent 5-input) Tj
T*
(   LUTs sharing inputs. In SliceM, LUTs can be configured as 64-bit distributed RAM or 32-bit) Tj
T*
(   shift registers \(SRL32\).) Tj
T*
(   - Flip-Flops: Each slice houses eight storage elements \(flip-flops/latches\) with configurable) Tj
T*
(   synchronous/asynchronous set, reset, and clock enable controls.) Tj
T*
