(   frequency resolution.) Tj
T*
(   - Logarithmic Amplifier & Envelope Detector: Detects the envelope amplitude of the IF signal on) Tj
T*
(   a logarithmic \(dBm\) scale.) Tj
T*
(   - Video Filter \(Video Bandwidth - VBW\): A lowpass smoothing filter positioned after the) Tj
T*
(   envelope detector to average out high-frequency trace noise on the display.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Resolution Bandwidth \(RBW\) Impact on Measurements:) Tj
T*
(   - Resolving Closely Spaced Signals: Two equal-amplitude sinusoidal signals separated by Delta f) Tj
T*
(   can only be displayed as distinct separate peaks if the RBW is less than or equal to Delta f.) Tj
T*
(   If RBW > Delta f, the peaks blur into a single composite peak.) Tj
T*
(   - Displayed Average Noise Level \(DANL\): Thermal noise power passing through the IF filter is) Tj
T*
(   proportional to bandwidth \(Noise = k * T * RBW\). Reducing RBW by a factor of 10 drops the noise) Tj
T*
(   floor by 10 dB \(10 * log10\(10\)\), revealing microscopic low-level signals previously buried in) Tj
T*
(   noise.) Tj
T*
(   - Sweep Time Trade-off: Narrowing RBW requires the LO to sweep much slower to allow the narrow) Tj
T*
(   IF filter to physically ring up to full amplitude: Sweep Time = k * \(Span\) / \(RBW^2\). Narrowing) Tj
T*
(   RBW by 10x increases sweep time by 100x!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Video Bandwidth \(VBW\) Function:) Tj
T*
(   - VBW does not change the average noise floor level; it acts as a lowpass post-detection) Tj
T*
(   smoothing filter. When VBW <= RBW / 10, noise fluctuations are averaged into a smooth,) Tj
T*
(   stationary baseline, making faint signals easily discernible.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
