(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles and architecture of Graphical System Design using National Instruments LabVIEW, detailing dataflow execution, Virtual Instruments \(VIs\), structures, and hardware interfacing \(DAQ\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Graphical System Design Paradigm:) Tj
T*
(   - National Instruments LabVIEW \(Laboratory Virtual Instrument Engineering Workbench\) is a) Tj
T*
(   premier engineering development environment built upon graphical programming \(known as 'G'\). It) Tj
T*
(   is widely utilized across aerospace, automotive, and telecommunications for automated test) Tj
T*
(   benches, laboratory instrumentation control, and industrial data acquisition \(DAQ\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Concepts: Virtual Instruments \(VIs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Front Panel: The user interface containing Controls \(knobs, switches, numeric inputs\)) Tj
T*
(   representing inputs, and Indicators \(graphs, meters, LEDs\) representing outputs.) Tj
T*
(   - Block Diagram: The underlying source code where graphical nodes \(functions, subVIs\) are) Tj
T*
(   interconnected by colored wires representing data types \(orange for floating-point, blue for) Tj
T*
(   integer, green for boolean, pink for string\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dataflow Execution Model:) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike text-based languages \(C, Python\) where instructions execute sequentially from top to) Tj
T*
(   bottom, LabVIEW programs execute according to dataflow principles. A node executes if and only) Tj
T*
(   if valid data has arrived at all of its required input terminals. Nodes that have their inputs) Tj
T*
(   satisfied can execute simultaneously, making parallel multi-threaded programming inherently) Tj
T*
(   intuitive and automatic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Execution Structures:) Tj
T*
