T*
(   2. Key DFM \(Design for Manufacturing\) Layout Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Minimum Trace Width and Spacing: Sized according to IPC-2152 thermal charts to ensure) Tj
T*
(   current-carrying copper traces do not exceed allowable temperature rise \(Delta T < 10 deg C\),) Tj
T*
(   while maintaining dielectric clearance to prevent voltage flashover.) Tj
T*
(   - Via and Annular Ring Integrity: Minimum annular ring \(the copper ring remaining around a) Tj
T*
(   drilled hole after etching\) must meet IPC Class 2 or Class 3 standards \(e.g. minimum 2 to 4) Tj
T*
(   mils after drill registration shift\) to prevent hole breakout that causes open circuits.) Tj
T*
(   - Aspect Ratio: Ratio of PCB board thickness to smallest mechanically drilled via diameter) Tj
T*
(   \(typically kept below 8:1 to 10:1\) to ensure copper electroplating solutions can penetrate and) Tj
T*
(   plate the barrel wall uniformly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. DFA \(Design for Assembly\) Guidelines:) Tj
T*
(   - Component Spacing & Orientation: Orient passive components \(0603, 0402 resistors/caps\) in) Tj
T*
(   identical directions to optimize automated high-speed surface-mount placement and reflow oven) Tj
T*
(   thermal heating.) Tj
T*
(   - Solder Bridging Prevention: Maintain minimum solder mask dams \(>= 3 to 4 mils\) between) Tj
T*
(   fine-pitch IC pins to prevent liquid solder bridges during wave or reflow soldering.) Tj
T*
(   - Fiducial Markers: Placing at least three optical copper fiducial marks on PCB corners to) Tj
T*
(   allow pick-and-place camera systems to optically align and correct board offset and rotation) Tj
T*
(   before component mounting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
