(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role and architecture of Hardware Description Language \(HDL\) High-Level Synthesis \(HLS\), detailing how C/C++ algorithms are transformed into synthesizable RTL, pragmas, and latency/throughput trade-offs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Motivation for High-Level Synthesis \(HLS\):) Tj
T*
(   - Traditional digital hardware design requires authoring detailed Register-Transfer Level \(RTL\)) Tj
T*
(   code in Verilog or VHDL, manually specifying every flip-flop, state machine, and clock cycle.) Tj
T*
(   As algorithms in computer vision, deep learning inference, and 5G signal processing become) Tj
T*
(   extraordinarily complex, manual RTL authoring becomes a severe bottleneck.) Tj
T*
(   - High-Level Synthesis \(e.g., AMD Xilinx Vitis HLS\) allows engineers to author algorithmic) Tj
T*
(   models in standard C, C++, or SystemC and automatically synthesizes them into cycle-accurate,) Tj
T*
(   synthesizable Verilog/VHDL netlists.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. HLS Compilation and Scheduling Lifecycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Parsing & Control Data Flow Graph \(CDFG\): Translates C code into an internal dependency graph) Tj
T*
(   where nodes represent arithmetic operations and edges represent data dependencies.) Tj
T*
(   - Scheduling: Assigns arithmetic operations to specific clock cycles based on target FPGA clock) Tj
T*
(   frequency \(e.g. 250 MHz\) and standard cell timing libraries.) Tj
T*
(   - Binding: Allocates physical hardware resources?mapping C array accesses to Block RAMs,) Tj
T*
(   mathematical multiplications to DSP48 slices, and variables to flip-flop registers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. HLS Optimization Pragmas:) Tj
T*
(   - Loop Pipelining \(`#pragma HLS pipeline`\): Allows subsequent loop iterations to begin before) Tj
T*
(   the current iteration finishes, reducing the Initiation Interval \(II\) to 1, achieving maximum) Tj
T*
(   throughput.) Tj
T*
(   - Loop Unrolling \(`#pragma HLS unroll`\): Replicates loop body hardware N times in parallel,) Tj
T*
(   trading increased silicon FPGA slice area for massive speedup.) Tj
T*
(   - Array Partitioning \(`#pragma HLS array_partition`\): Splits large C arrays into individual) Tj
T*
(   registers or multiple independent BRAM banks, eliminating memory port bottlenecks and allowing) Tj
T*
(   simultaneous parallel access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 21:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
