(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture, measurement techniques, and circuit topology of an Arbitrary Waveform Generator \(AWG\), detailing Direct Digital Synthesis \(DDS\), DAC resolution, phase noise, and anti-aliasing reconstruction.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Architecture of an Arbitrary Waveform Generator \(AWG\):) Tj
T*
(   - An AWG is a precision electronic test instrument that synthesizes completely arbitrary,) Tj
T*
(   user-defined voltage waveforms?from pristine standard sine/square waves to complex multi-tone) Tj
T*
(   RF chirps, radar pulses, and automotive sensor simulation signals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Direct Digital Synthesis \(DDS\) Operational Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Accumulator: A high-speed N-bit digital counter \(typically 32 to 48 bits\). On every) Tj
T*
(   clock cycle of a precision reference oscillator \(f_clk\), a user-defined Frequency Tuning Word) Tj
T*
(   \(FTW / M\) is added to the accumulator: Phase_new = \(Phase_old + M\) mod 2^N.) Tj
T*
(   - Output Frequency Equation: The synthesized output frequency is mathematically: f_out = \( M *) Tj
T*
(   f_clk \) / \(2^N\). This yields microhertz frequency resolution.) Tj
T*
(   - Phase-to-Amplitude Mapping: The upper bits of the phase accumulator address a Waveform Memory) Tj
T*
(   \(Look-Up Table\) containing digital amplitude samples of the desired waveform.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Digital-to-Analog Conversion and Reconstruction Filtering:) Tj
T*
(   - High-Speed DAC: Converts digital amplitude samples into a continuous staircase analog voltage) Tj
T*
(   waveform. DAC resolution \(typically 14 to 16 bits\) dictates dynamic range and Spurious-Free) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic Range \(SFDR\).) Tj
T*
(   - Anti-Aliasing Reconstruction Filter: A sharp low-pass analog filter that removes) Tj
T*
(   high-frequency DAC sampling images and Nyquist aliases \(f_clk - f_out, f_clk + f_out\),) Tj
T*
(   smoothing the staircase into an ultra-pure, low-distortion analog waveform.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
