T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. DO-254 \(Design Assurance Guidance for Airborne Electronic Hardware\):) Tj
T*
(   - Applies to complex electronic hardware \(ASICs, FPGAs, PLDs\) installed on aircraft.) Tj
T*
(   - Design Assurance Levels \(DAL\): Ranging from DAL A \(Catastrophic - failure prevents safe) Tj
T*
(   flight and landing, e.g. primary flight computers\) down to DAL E \(No safety effect, e.g.) Tj
T*
(   passenger in-flight entertainment\).) Tj
T*
(   - Strict Requirements Traceability: Every single line of RTL code, pin connection, and state) Tj
T*
(   machine transition must trace directly back to a validated high-level system requirement.) Tj
T*
(   Unintended or undocumented hardware functions are strictly illegal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Hardware Fault Tolerance in Aerospace:) Tj
T*
(   - Triple Modular Redundancy \(TMR\): Triplicating critical hardware compute blocks and voting on) Tj
T*
(   outputs via hardware majority logic to survive single-event radiation upsets \(SEUs\) caused by) Tj
T*
(   cosmic rays at high altitudes.) Tj
T*
(   - Dissimilar Redundancy: Implementing backup flight computers using completely different) Tj
T*
(   processor architectures and different compilers to prevent common-mode software bugs from) Tj
T*
(   disabling the aircraft.) Tj
T*
() Tj
