12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles and syntax of SystemVerilog Functional Coverage, detailing covergroups, coverpoints, bins, cross-coverage, and how coverage metrics guide verification closure.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Concept of Functional Coverage Closure:) Tj
T*
(   - Code coverage measures whether RTL code lines and branches were executed by simulation;) Tj
T*
(   however, 100% code coverage does NOT mean the design is bug-free \(e.g. missing requirements) Tj
T*
(   will never show up in code coverage\). Functional coverage measures whether the hardware has) Tj
T*
(   been tested against the human-authored functional specifications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Syntax and Structure of Functional Coverage:) Tj
T*
(   - Covergroup Definition: Encloses coverage metrics, instantiated within classes or interfaces,) Tj
T*
(   triggered by clock events or sampling functions:) Tj
T*
(   covergroup cg_packet @\(posedge clk\);) Tj
T*
(   cp_length: coverpoint pkt.length {) Tj
T*
(   bins min_pkt = {64};) Tj
T*
(   bins mid_pkt = {[65:1500]};) Tj
T*
(   bins max_pkt = {1518};) Tj
T*
(   bins jumbo = {[1519:9000]};) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   cp_dest_port: coverpoint pkt.dest_port {) Tj
T*
(   bins port_0 = {0};) Tj
T*
(   bins port_1 = {1};) Tj
T*
(   bins others = default;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   // Cross-Coverage:) Tj
T*
(   cross_len_port: cross cp_length, cp_dest_port;) Tj
T*
(   endgroup) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Cross-Coverage and Corner-Case Exploration:) Tj
T*
(   - Cross coverage creates a Cartesian product of two or more coverpoints, tracking whether every) Tj
T*
(   combination \(e.g. jumbo packet sent to port 0 while buffer is 99% full\) has occurred during) Tj
T*
(   simulation.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
