(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture, hardware components, and firmware design of an Electric Vehicle \(EV\) Motor Controller using Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\), detailing Clarke and Park transformations, PWM, and gate drivers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Motor Control Challenges in Modern EVs:) Tj
T*
(   - Modern electric vehicles utilize Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motors \(PMSM\) or AC Induction) Tj
T*
(   Motors for propulsion. To deliver smooth torque from zero speed, eliminate audible motor whine,) Tj
T*
(   and maximize energy efficiency during regenerative braking, controllers must decouple complex) Tj
T*
(   AC stator magnetic fields in real time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Mathematical Architecture of Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stator Current Measurement: Precision shunt resistors or Hall-effect sensors measure) Tj
T*
(   instantaneous 3-phase AC currents \(Ia, Ib, Ic\).) Tj
T*
(   - Clarke Transformation: Transforms 3-phase stationary coordinates \(Ia, Ib, Ic\) into a 2-phase) Tj
T*
(   stationary orthogonal reference frame \(I_alpha, I_beta\):) Tj
T*
(   I_alpha = Ia; I_beta = \(Ia + 2 * Ib\) / sqrt\(3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Park Transformation: Rotates the stationary orthogonal currents into a rotating reference) Tj
T*
(   frame aligned with the rotor's permanent magnetic flux vector \(at rotor angle theta measured by) Tj
T*
(   an encoder\):) Tj
T*
(   I_d = I_alpha * cos\(theta\) + I_beta * sin\(theta\); \(Direct Axis Current - governs magnetic flux\)) Tj
T*
(   I_q = -I_alpha * sin\(theta\) + I_beta * cos\(theta\); \(Quadrature Axis Current - governs) Tj
T*
(   mechanical torque\)) Tj
T*
(   - Decoupled PI Control: Independent Proportional-Integral \(PI\) controllers regulate I_d) Tj
T*
(   \(commanded to 0 for maximum torque-per-ampere\) and I_q \(proportional to accelerator pedal) Tj
T*
(   torque demand\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inverse Park & Space Vector PWM \(SVPWM\): Transforms regulated control voltages back to stator) Tj
T*
(   coordinates, driving 6-switch power MOSFET/IGBT inverter bridges with maximum DC bus voltage) Tj
T*
(   utilization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 26:) Tj
T*
