(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture, hardware components, and software protocols of an Industrial IoT Predictive Maintenance System, detailing triaxial vibration sensors, edge FFT processing, and MQTT cloud telemetry.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Predictive Maintenance in Industry 4.0:) Tj
T*
(   - Industrial manufacturing facilities operate critical rotating machinery?turbines, pumps,) Tj
T*
(   compressors, and CNC spindles. Unplanned bearing or gear failures cause massive financial) Tj
T*
(   losses. Predictive maintenance systems detect microscopic mechanical wear months before) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Sensor Hardware and Edge Signal Processing:) Tj
T*
(   - Triaxial Piezoelectric / MEMS Accelerometers: Sized to capture high-bandwidth physical) Tj
T*
(   vibrations \(up to 10 kHz to 20 kHz\) with low noise density \(<50 micro-g/sqrt\(Hz\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - Edge FFT Processing: An on-node 32-bit ARM Cortex-M7 or DSP microcontroller samples vibration) Tj
T*
(   signals at 40 kSa/s. Instead of streaming raw gigabytes of time-domain data over wireless) Tj
T*
(   networks, the edge processor executes an onboard 2048-point Fast Fourier Transform \(FFT\).) Tj
T*
(   - Spectral Defect Feature Extraction: Evaluates peak vibration amplitudes at specific) Tj
T*
(   mechanical fault frequencies: Ball Pass Frequency Outer Race \(BPFO\), Ball Pass Frequency Inner) Tj
T*
(   Race \(BPFI\), and gear mesh frequencies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Low-Power Telemetry & Cloud Dashboards:) Tj
T*
(   - Wireless Transmission: Transmits compressed spectral defect summaries over LoRaWAN or NB-IoT) Tj
T*
(   using lightweight MQTT \(Message Queuing Telemetry Transport\) publish-subscribe protocols over) Tj
T*
(   TLS security to cloud monitoring dashboards.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
